<Layout title="Nous application — Javier Ponz" description="Javier Ponz's open application to Nous Research." dark><section class="hero"><p class="kicker">Open application</p><h1>Why I am looking at <span class="serif">Nous</span>.</h1><p class="lede">A personal application, published openly. I am not affiliated with, sponsored by or employed by Nous Research.</p></section><section class="grid"><span class="label">The fit I see</span><div class="copy"><h2>Adoption, enablement and hard feedback.</h2><p>I have spent the last stretch operating Hermes Agent and OpenClaw daily — building automations, running them in Docker, breaking them, and documenting the failure modes. That is the kind of use that produces useful product feedback: not what the docs say should happen, but what actually happens on the fourth attempt at 1am.</p><p>Behind that sits ten years at Apple Retail doing technical diagnosis and customer operations at scale, and a current transition into AI systems and full stack development with shipped, deployed work to show for it.</p><p>Forward-deployed or product-facing enablement look like the most honest fit for that combination today, and I am equally interested in where someone with a clearer view of the org would place it.</p></div></section><section class="grid"><span class="label">What I bring</span><div class="cards"><article class="card"><span class="meta">01</span><h3>Real usage</h3><p>Daily operation of agent systems, with the debugging notes and failure traces that come from it.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="meta">02</span><h3>Translation</h3><p>Ten years turning technical complexity into something a non-technical person can act on.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="meta">03</span><h3>Written evidence</h3><p>Public repositories, tests, release gates and a live deployment — all inspectable.</p></article></div></section><section class="grid"><span class="label">Conversation</span><div class="copy"><p>For a conversation, contact me at <a href="mailto:nerion89@gmail.com?subject=Javier%20Ponz%20—%20Nous%20application">nerion89@gmail.com</a>. The official careers context is at <a href="https://nousresearch.com/careers" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Nous Research Careers ↗</a>.</p></div></section></Layout>
